
Release workflow security and validation contract
  shares the same full validation for PRs, branches and tags with read-only defaults
  limits write permissions to tag publication and never inherits PR secrets
  has full release-line history with non-persisted credentials and Node24 checkout
  does not cancel publication or collide caller and reusable concurrency groups
  sets an executable Linux Helm path and registers the repository before locked build
  resolves all four exact maintenance cells outside source without ignoring Bundler config
  gives setup-ruby an existing Gemfile before publishing the private matrix manifest
  generates the QA-aligned test-only diff-lcs bound outside the unchanged source Gemfile
  packages only after complete RSpec and Cucumber success and passes immutable artifact identity
  allows main recovery and limits the exact maintenance controller to 1.x tags
  fails the required gate for failed, cancelled, skipped or missing matrix results
  checks stable tags and the controller checkout against its fixed trusted remote before source or API lookup
  requires a completed original tag validation and retained immutable artifacts for draft recovery
  rechecks the original tag and release ancestry in the recovery source before publication tooling runs
  reuses original immutable artifacts and source rather than rebuilding an existing tag

